---
import SectionHeading from "./CaseSectionHeading.astro";
import MediaFrame from "./ProductMediaFrame.astro";
import AnimatedGif from "./AnimatedGif.astro";
import ScrollableMediaFrame from "./ScrollableMediaFrame.astro";
import CampaignFlowGraphic from "./CampaignFlowGraphic.astro";
import originalArtboards from "../assets/campaign-builder/graphics/campaign-original-artboards.png";
import fullCampaign from "../assets/campaign-builder/graphics/campaign-full-campaign-tall-scrolable.png";
import generationGif from "../assets/gifs/campaign-builder/campaign-fast-asset-demo.gif?url";
import generationStill from "../assets/gifs/campaign-builder/campaign-fast-asset-demo-still.png";
import exportGif from "../assets/gifs/campaign-builder/campaign-final-assets-preorganized.gif?url";
import exportStill from "../assets/gifs/campaign-builder/campaign-final-assets-preorganized-still.png";
import currentWorkspace from "../assets/campaign-builder/graphics/campaign-current-workspace-hero.png";
---

<div class="campaign-quick">
  <section id="overview">
    <SectionHeading number="01" eyebrow="Overview" title="A reusable system for building coordinated campaign assets." />
    <p class="ownership">I created and built Campaign Builder end to end.</p>
    <p class="section-intro">I owned problem definition, the first working design system, product strategy, UX/UI, application development, reusable template rules, presentation and export workflows, rollout, and testing.</p>
    <div class="overview-context">
      <div><span>Source model</span><strong>Three shared image shapes</strong></div>
      <div><span>Current use</span><strong>OGIO and CGPO designers</strong></div>
      <div><span>Rollout</span><strong>Callaway adoption beginning</strong></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="problem">
    <SectionHeading number="02" eyebrow="The problem" title="One campaign meant maintaining many separate artboards." />
    <p class="section-intro">Homepage, email, paid media, remarketing, merchandising, and tile assets were built separately. A change could mean repeated edits across formats, extra presentation work for approval, and another round of manual organization before downstream teams could use the files.</p>
    <MediaFrame label="Original multi-artboard workflow">
      <img src={originalArtboards.src} width={originalArtboards.width} height={originalArtboards.height} alt="Original Figma campaign workspace showing many separately maintained desktop and mobile artboards." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </MediaFrame>
  </section>

  <section id="built">
    <SectionHeading number="03" eyebrow="What I built" title="Three source-image shapes can drive a coordinated campaign family." />
    <p class="section-intro">Campaign Builder separates the content that changes for each campaign—copy, imagery, logos, and variations—from reusable system rules for dimensions, typography, spacing, positioning, and templates.</p>
    <CampaignFlowGraphic />
    <MediaFrame label="Current campaign workspace">
      <img src={currentWorkspace.src} width={currentWorkspace.width} height={currentWorkspace.height} alt="Current Campaign Builder workspace showing shared campaign controls, variations, export selections, and coordinated previews." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </MediaFrame>
    <div class="story-beat">
      <div><p>01 · Create faster</p><h3>Load shared imagery and generate coordinated outputs.</h3><p>The interaction shows tall, wide, and skinny source images being applied across the campaign workspace, followed by a switch between variations.</p></div>
      <MediaFrame label="Source images to campaign outputs" motion>
        <AnimatedGif src={generationGif} fallbackSrc={generationStill.src} width={generationStill.width} height={generationStill.height} alt="Campaign Builder interaction showing shared source images being applied across campaign formats and a switch between variations." />
      </MediaFrame>
    </div>
    <div class="presentation-story">
      <p>02 · Approve faster</p>
      <h3>Review the campaign as one coordinated presentation.</h3>
      <p>The presentation view brings web, mobile, email, paid media, and secondary formats together so the direction can be reviewed as a system.</p>
      <ScrollableMediaFrame label="Full campaign presentation" accessibleLabel="Scrollable full campaign presentation containing coordinated web, mobile, email, paid media, and secondary formats.">
        <img src={fullCampaign.src} width={fullCampaign.width} height={fullCampaign.height} alt="Campaign Builder presentation mode showing a coordinated campaign across web, mobile, email, paid media, and secondary formats." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </ScrollableMediaFrame>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="impact">
    <SectionHeading number="04" eyebrow="Impact" title="Less repeated production work, with faster ways to explore and finish a campaign." />
    <div class="impact-grid">
      <div class="primary-impact"><strong>~75%</strong><span>estimated production-time reduction</span></div>
      <div><strong>~10 min</strong><span>approximate final variation setup once source imagery is ready</span></div>
      <div><strong>Under 30 min</strong><span>for concept exploration</span></div>
      <div><strong>Current</strong><span>designer usage with broader rollout beginning</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="impact-note">These are working estimates based on the current workflow, not a formal time study. Concept exploration timing is separate from final variation setup once imagery is ready.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="why">
    <SectionHeading number="05" eyebrow="Why it worked" title="The system addressed the workflow, not only the artboards." />
    <blockquote>A design system can standardize the work without actually fixing the workflow.</blockquote>
    <p class="section-intro">The key decision was to connect creation, presentation, and delivery. Reusable rules reduce repeated setup; one presentation view keeps approval connected to the campaign; and one export creates a cleaner downstream handoff.</p>
    <div class="delivery-story">
      <div><p>03 · Deliver cleaner</p><h3>One campaign becomes one organized export.</h3><p>The exported files are grouped by channel and use, with consistent filenames that make the intended output easier to find.</p></div>
      <MediaFrame label="Organized downstream handoff" motion>
        <AnimatedGif src={exportGif} fallbackSrc={exportStill.src} width={exportStill.width} height={exportStill.height} alt="Exported Campaign Builder assets organized into email, paid, and web folders with consistent filenames." />
      </MediaFrame>
    </div>
    <div class="deep-dive-cta">
      <div><p>Extended reading</p><h3>Explore the Figma V1, source-image model, system rules, controls, rollout, and future direction.</h3></div>
      <button class="button-link" type="button" data-deep-toggle aria-controls="deep-dive" aria-expanded="false"><span data-deep-toggle-label>Read the Deep Dive</span> <span data-deep-toggle-icon aria-hidden="true">↓</span></button>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .campaign-quick > section { padding-block: var(--space-8); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--header-height) + var(--space-7)); }
  .ownership { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); font-size: var(--step-2); font-weight: 680; line-height: 1.25; }
  .section-intro { margin: 0 0 var(--space-6); color: var(--color-text-soft); font-size: var(--step-1); }
  .overview-context { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin-top: var(--space-6); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .overview-context div { display: grid; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .overview-context div:first-child { padding-left: 0; }
  .overview-context div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .overview-context span, .impact-grid span { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .overview-context strong { font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .story-beat { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-7); }
  .story-beat > div { max-width: 46rem; }
  .story-beat :global(.media-frame) { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  .delivery-story { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-5); align-items: start; margin-top: var(--space-7); }
  .story-beat > div > p:first-child, .presentation-story > p:first-child, .delivery-story > div > p:first-child { margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); color: var(--color-accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.64rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .story-beat h3, .presentation-story h3, .delivery-story h3 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); font-size: var(--step-2); }
  .story-beat > div > p:last-child, .presentation-story > p, .delivery-story > div > p:last-child { color: var(--color-text-soft); }
  .presentation-story { margin-top: var(--space-8); padding-top: var(--space-7); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .presentation-story > p:not(:first-child) { max-width: 54rem; }
  .presentation-story :global(.scrollable-media-frame) { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  blockquote { margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); padding-left: var(--space-4); border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent); font-size: var(--step-2); font-weight: 680; line-height: 1.25; }
  .impact-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); }
  .impact-grid > div { display: flex; min-height: 11rem; flex-direction: column; padding: var(--space-5); border-right: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .impact-grid > div:nth-child(2n) { border-right: 0; }
  .impact-grid strong { margin-top: auto; color: var(--color-accent); font-kerning: normal; font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 4rem); letter-spacing: -0.025em; line-height: 0.95; }
  .impact-grid span { margin-top: var(--space-3); line-height: 1.45; }
  .impact-grid .primary-impact { grid-row: span 2; min-height: 22rem; }
  .impact-grid .primary-impact strong { font-size: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem); }
  .impact-note { margin: 0; padding: var(--space-5); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 5%, transparent); color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .delivery-story { margin-top: var(--space-7); padding-top: var(--space-7); border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .delivery-story :global(.motion .media-window) { aspect-ratio: 341 / 199; }
  .deep-dive-cta { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: var(--space-6); margin-top: var(--space-8); padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong); background: var(--color-surface); }
  .deep-dive-cta p { margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); color: var(--color-text-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.07em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .deep-dive-cta h3 { max-width: 34rem; margin: 0; }
  .deep-dive-cta .button-link { flex: 0 0 auto; }

  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .overview-context { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .overview-context div { padding-inline: 0; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
    .overview-context div:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
    .impact-grid .primary-impact { grid-row: auto; min-height: 11rem; }
    .deep-dive-cta { align-items: stretch; flex-direction: column; }
  }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .impact-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .impact-grid > div { min-height: 9rem; border-right: 0; }
  }
</style>
